From: YamadaBlog <118530756+YamadaBlog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 15:39:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 22/30] Niri scroll: verify the size writes of animation ticks
 so later ticks move windows only

Animation ticks write position only once a window's size is verified, but ticks never verify,
so a window whose size was unverified (e.g. a column revealed from parking) re-wrote its size,
unverified, on every tick of the scroll; Safari then re-laid out its page every frame. Verify
the ticks' size writes; position-only writes stay unverified.
---
 .../OmniWM/Core/Controller/LayoutDiffExecutor.swift   | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Sources/OmniWM/Core/Controller/LayoutDiffExecutor.swift b/Sources/OmniWM/Core/Controller/LayoutDiffExecutor.swift
index b19da82b..fee50329 100644
--- a/Sources/OmniWM/Core/Controller/LayoutDiffExecutor.swift
+++ b/Sources/OmniWM/Core/Controller/LayoutDiffExecutor.swift
@@ -122,7 +122,16 @@ final class LayoutDiffExecutor {
             }
         }
         guard isInteractiveResize else {
-            axManager.applyFramesParallel(frameUpdates, verify: !isAnimationTick)
+            guard isAnimationTick else {
+                axManager.applyFramesParallel(frameUpdates, verify: true)
+                return
+            }
+            // Animation ticks write position only once a window's size is verified (animationFrameComponents).
+            // An unverified size was otherwise re-written, unverified, on every tick of the scroll: Safari then
+            // re-laid out its page each frame (2026-10-16 bench: one column wrote its size on ~95 % of ticks).
+            // Verify those size writes so the next ticks move the window only.
+            axManager.applyFramesParallel(frameUpdates.filter { $0.components == .position }, verify: false)
+            axManager.applyFramesParallel(frameUpdates.filter { $0.components != .position }, verify: true)
             return
         }
         let moves = frameUpdates.filter { $0.components == .position }
